+
+### `applyMergePatch(target, patch)`
+
+Applies a [JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386) (RFC 7386) to a JSON `target`
+document and returns the merged document as a new value, without mutating `target`.
+
+- `target`: any JSON-compatible value.
+- `patch`: any JSON-compatible value. An object member merges recursively into the corresponding
+  member of `target`; a `null` member removes the corresponding member from the result; any other
+  patch value (including an array, `null`, or a scalar) replaces the corresponding part of `target`
+  outright.
+
+Every JSON value is a valid merge patch, so, unlike `applyPatch`, this function never throws.
